Hi chia,

Thank you for the thoughtful feedback!

chia_10: I have added a clarification in the Proposed Changes section to =
address this. In this case,
 ListOffsetsRequest will resolve to the Log End Offset, but this is not =
a fallback to `latest`. The distinction=20
matters: `latest` is a direct seek to the Log End Offset, whereas =
`by_start_time` always anchors to the=20
group creation timestamp and lets the lookup result follow naturally. =
The consumer will begin consuming=20
any new records produced after this point normally.

chia_11: I have introduced a new exception =
`GroupCreationTimeUnknownException` to signal=20
this specific condition.

chia_12: I have updated the KIP to expose the group creation timestamp =
via `AdminClient.describeConsumerGroups()`
, accessible through `ConsumerGroupDescription.groupCreationTimeMs()`. =
This is backed by a new=20
`GroupCreationTimeMs` field in `ConsumerGroupDescribeResponse.

Best Regards,
Jiunn-Yang

> Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@apache.org> =E6=96=BC 2026=E5=B9=B44=E6=9C=881=E6=
=97=A5 =E4=B8=8B=E5=8D=882:33 =E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
>=20
> hi Jiunn
>=20
> thanks for updating KIP. I have a couple of questions.
>=20
> chia_10: What happen if the group creation time is strictly greater =
than the timestamp of the latest record in the partition? Will the =
consumer fall back to the "latest" offset behaviour in this case? It =
could be good to elucidate that in the KIP
>=20
> chia_11: Could you specify which exact exception will be thrown when =
the group creation time is unknown
>=20
> chia_12: Since the group creation time is now a critical semantic =
anchor, should we also expose it via the `DescribeGroupsResponse`?
>=20
> Best,
> Chia-Ping
>=20
> On 2026/03/05 11:14:31 =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD wrote:
>> Hello everyone,=20
>>=20
>> I would like to start a discussion on KIP-1282: Prevent data loss =
during partition expansion for dynamically added partitions
>> <https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/mIY8G>
>>=20
>> This proposal aims to introduce a new auto.offset.reset policy =
by_start_time, anchoring the=20
>> offset reset to the consumer's startup timestamp rather than =
partition discovery time, to prevent=20
>> silent data loss during partition expansion.
>>=20
>> Best regards,
>> Jiunn-Yang


