>=20
> hi Jiunn
>=20
> chia_13: should we update the public API: ConsumerGroupDescription as =
well?
>=20
> Best,
> Chia-Ping
>=20
> On 2026/04/01 11:59:46 =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD wrote:
>> Hi chia,
>>=20
>> Thank you for the thoughtful feedback!
>>=20
>> chia_10: I have added a clarification in the Proposed Changes section =
to address this. In this case,
>> ListOffsetsRequest will resolve to the Log End Offset, but this is =
not a fallback to `latest`. The distinction=20
>> matters: `latest` is a direct seek to the Log End Offset, whereas =
`by_start_time` always anchors to the=20
>> group creation timestamp and lets the lookup result follow naturally. =
The consumer will begin consuming=20
>> any new records produced after this point normally.
>>=20
>> chia_11: I have introduced a new exception =
`GroupCreationTimeUnknownException` to signal=20
>> this specific condition.
>>=20
>> chia_12: I have updated the KIP to expose the group creation =
timestamp via `AdminClient.describeConsumerGroups()`
>> , accessible through =
`ConsumerGroupDescription.groupCreationTimeMs()`. This is backed by a =
new=20
>> `GroupCreationTimeMs` field in `ConsumerGroupDescribeResponse.
>>=20
>> Best Regards,
>> Jiunn-Yang
>>=20
