>>>=20
>>> hi Jiunn
>>>=20
>>> thanks for updating KIP. I have a couple of questions.
>>>=20
>>> chia_10: What happen if the group creation time is strictly greater =
than the timestamp of the latest record in the partition? Will the =
consumer fall back to the "latest" offset behaviour in this case? It =
could be good to elucidate that in the KIP
>>>=20
>>> chia_11: Could you specify which exact exception will be thrown when =
the group creation time is unknown
>>>=20
>>> chia_12: Since the group creation time is now a critical semantic =
anchor, should we also expose it via the `DescribeGroupsResponse`?
>>>=20
>>> Best,
>>> Chia-Ping
>>>=20
>>> On 2026/03/05 11:14:31 =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD wrote:
>>>> Hello everyone,=20
>>>>=20
>>>> I would like to start a discussion on KIP-1282: Prevent data loss =
during partition expansion for dynamically added partitions
>>>> <https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/mIY8G>
>>>>=20
>>>> This proposal aims to introduce a new auto.offset.reset policy =
by_start_time, anchoring the=20
>>>> offset reset to the consumer's startup timestamp rather than =
partition discovery time, to prevent=20
>>>> silent data loss during partition expansion.
>>>>=20
>>>> Best regards,
