>=20
> =EF=BB=BFHi Aditya,
> I agree that using the existing ConsumerRebalanceListener gives a lower ad=
option burden.
>=20
> AS1: To be more concrete with what I mean here, we could:
> * Deprecate Consumer.subscribe(Collection<String>, ConsumerRebalanceListen=
er) for removal in AK 5.0
> * Introduce Consumer.setConsumerRebalanceListener(ConsumerRebalanceListene=
r)
>=20
> AS2: Given that we already have an interface called ConsumerRebalanceListe=
ner, I suggest that ConsumerRebalanceXXX would be a better naming choice for=
 naming your new interface in terms of consistency.
>=20
> Thanks,
> Andrew
>=20
