Fabian Bell created KAFKA-20416:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: RocksDB loses entries during broker patches.
                 Key: KAFKA-20416
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20416
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 3.9.1
         Environment: MSK with kafka.m7g.2xlarge instances
            Reporter: Fabian Bell


h2. Problem:

We discovered a strange behaviour on our production environment. We use a K=
Table to look up data from a topic we write to.

=C2=A0
{code:java}
builder.table(topicName, Consumed.with(keySerde, valueSerde), Materialized.=
as(storeName)) {code}
=C2=A0
When we access the store in the processor, we observed that the store retur=
ned null values for keys that have non-null entries in the topic that backs=
 the KTable after an MSK security patch. We never tombstone an entry in our=
 topic nor have a delete retention activated.
This only happens for some of our instances.
We see the following stream logs:
=C2=A0
{code:java}
Committing task(s) 0_14 failed.
Detected the states of tasks [0_14] are corrupted. Will close the task as d=
irty and re-create and bootstrap from scratch.
Active task(s) got corrupted. Triggering a rebalance.
End offset for changelog our-topic-14 initialized as 16596290.
Restoration in progress for 1 partitions. {our-topic-14: position=3D0, end=
=3D16596290, totalRestored=3D0}
State transition from RUNNING to PARTITIONS_REVOKED
No followup rebalance was requested, resetting the rebalance schedule.
partition revocation took 80 ms.
State transition from PARTITIONS_REVOKED to PARTITIONS_ASSIGNED
State transition from PARTITIONS_ASSIGNED to RUNNING {code}
=C2=A0
This all happens within a few seconds, and the `Restoration in progress ...=
` log is the only one we can see. A full restoration usually takes like 30 =
min.=C2=A0
The error message of the commit failure is=C2=A0

{code:java}
o.a.k.c.e.TimeoutException: Timeout expired after 60000ms while awaiting Ad=
dOffsetsToTxn {code}
We can fix this situation by clearing the state directory and forcing a ful=
l restoration.
h2. Context:

Each instance has its own persistent state directory. The configured state =
directory does=C2=A0 not change.=C2=A0=C2=A0
Processing Guarantee: exactly_once_v2



