Subject: Re: Migrating system tests from Ducktape to Java/Testcontainers
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
From: Mickael Maison <mickael.maison@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Hi,

I'd really be in favor of replacing our Python system test framework
with something in Java.

> How would the new framework handle these older compatibility tests?

The tests for releases older than 3.7.0 will have to stay as is.
We would need to have both frameworks in parallel.

Even if this would not be changing any public APIs, we could do a KIP
if we want to have a formal vote.
But I wonder if more inputs from the community would be preferable
first. Are there any features/behavior of ducktape or the current
framework in general really important or liked?

Thanks,
Mickael


