Bill Bejeck created KAFKA-20467:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: KIP-892: Add BatchedDBAccessor to RocksDBStore for wr=
ite buffering
                 Key: KAFKA-20467
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20467
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
          Components: streams
            Reporter: Bill Bejeck
             Fix For: 4.4.0


Add BatchedDBAccessor inner class to RocksDBStore alongside existing Direct=
DBAccessor.

=C2=A0 - BatchedDBAccessor wraps a WriteBatchWithIndex: put/delete go to ba=
tch, get uses getFromBatchAndDB() for read-your-writes
=C2=A0 - commit(): write batch atomically to RocksDB (data + offsets in one=
 db.write(batch) call), then clear batch
=C2=A0 - rollback(): discard batch on task corruption
=C2=A0 - Track uncommittedBytes =E2=80=94 increment on every put/delete, re=
set on commit
=C2=A0 - approximateNumUncommittedBytes() returns tracked value
=C2=A0 - Accessor choice controlled by isolation level passed at store crea=
tion
=C2=A0 - Ensure batched accessor works with RocksDBTimestampedStore dual-CF=
 layout
=C2=A0 - Update RocksDbIterator to use WriteBatchWithIndex.newIteratorWithB=
ase() for merged iteration



