Bill Bejeck created KAFKA-20471:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: KIP-892: Implement Generic Transaction Buffer (Phase =
0)
                 Key: KAFKA-20471
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20471
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Bill Bejeck


Deliver the TransactionBuffer abstraction as a standalone, independently me=
rgeable piece before KIP-892 core work begins. This must land and stabilize=
 before Phase 1 begins. Can proceed in parallel with the StateStore.java in=
terface design.

Files to create:
- state/internals/TransactionBuffer.java =E2=80=94 interface
- state/internals/AbstractTransactionBuffer.java =E2=80=94 shared Concurren=
tSkipListMap + ReentrantReadWriteLock logic
- state/internals/RocksDBTransactionBuffer.java =E2=80=94 RocksDB implement=
ation (plain WriteBatch)
- state/internals/InMemoryTransactionBuffer.java =E2=80=94 in-memory implem=
entation
- state/internals/StagedMergeIterator.java =E2=80=94 merge iterator over st=
aging snapshot + base iterator

Files to modify:
- StreamsConfig.java =E2=80=94 add transactional.state.stores boolean confi=
g
- state/internals/RocksDBStore.java =E2=80=94 add TransactionalDBAccessor i=
nner class; wire in init()
- state/internals/InMemoryKeyValueStore.java =E2=80=94 wire InMemoryTransac=
tionBuffer in init()

Unit tests:
- RocksDBTransactionBufferTest =E2=80=94 stage/get/commit/rollback, cross-t=
hread read correctness
- InMemoryTransactionBufferTest =E2=80=94 same for in-memory
- StagedMergeIteratorTest =E2=80=94 overlapping keys, tombstones, ordering
- TransactionBufferConcurrencyTest =E2=80=94 concurrent scan creation vs. c=
ommit, no duplicates

Integration tests:
- RocksDBStoreWithGTBIntegrationTest =E2=80=94 IQ sees staged writes before=
 commit; committed state correct after



