Hi Andrew,

Sorry for the late reply and thanks for the feedback!

The original motivation behind this KIP is based on KAFKA-20144: that users w=
ho only have DESCRIBE on the cluster, but not DESCRIBE_CONFIGS were hitting t=
he issue described in KAFKA-20111. And thanks for your fix and for proposing =
KAFKA-20144 to address this.

That said, Chia-Ping and I found that handling both DESCRIBE and DESCRIBE_CON=
FIGS privileges in handleListConfigResources gets messy which is exactly why =
we proposed replacing DESCRIBE_CONFIGS with DESCRIBE there, to simplify the l=
ogic.

If we revert to DESCRIBE_CONFIGS, we're essentially keeping the current imple=
mentation as-is - which, from my perspective, doesn't address the user experi=
ence problem that motivated KAFKA-20144 in the first place.

Best,
Kuan-Po Tseng

