hi all,

Just a note for a potential latest_v2:

Since the purpose is to read all records from extended partitions, we could l=
everage the group creation time to compare against the earliest record of a p=
artition when there is no committed offset. If the group creation time is lar=
ger than the earliest record's timestamp, we assume it is not an extended par=
tition. Otherwise, we treat it as an extended partition.

This approach allows us to catch all "possible" extended partitions, which in=
cludes both "true" extended partitions and old but truncated partitions. Whil=
e there is a rare edge case where the cost is reprocessing some records we do=
n't necessarily want, it is very easy to implement and guarantees we will nev=
er miss the actual extended partitions.

Best,
Chia-Ping

