Hi Lianet,

Thanks for the review.

LM1: My intent was to leave the existing behaviour unchanged and support bot=
h methods equally. For users who upgrade to the new version, subscribe() wil=
l break on day 1 if we change default implementation to throw IllegalStateEx=
ception. The only change I was planning was to manually register the rebalan=
ce listener with the subscription state in the deprecated methods, where rig=
ht now we simply pass the listener as an argument.=20

LM2: I read the @Deprecated annotation as the version from which the method w=
ill stick around deprecated i.e. =E2=80=9Csince 4.4=E2=80=9D, but marked for=
 eventual removal at a future unspecified version (5.0/6.0).

LM3: Thanks for highlighting the missing methods. I=E2=80=99ve addressed the=
m in the updated included/excluded section. I=E2=80=99ve also added the inte=
rface for the new view in the KIP. It=E2=80=99s meant to mirror the methods o=
f Consumer -> KafkaConsumer by delegating the actual calls to the proper imp=
lementation.

LM4: I agree with the naming challenge. Some of the alternatives I=E2=80=99d=
 considered/rejected: RebalanceHandler, RebalanceView, ConsumerRebalanceView=
, GuardedConsumerView. We landed on ConsumerRebalanceAdapter since it=E2=80=99=
s not really just a view (we allow pause/commit etc.); we already have Consu=
merRebalanceListener so consistency played a role there.=20

I had not considered RebalanceConsumer. It fits here because it supports nea=
rly 70% of the methods on Consumer and clearly denotes it=E2=80=99s meant fo=
r use at rebalance time like you said. I agree with this change. I=E2=80=99v=
e updated the KIP with the new name.

Best,
Aditya

