Hi Jun,

Thanks for the feedback. I agree that shifting this policy toward a "Smarter=
 Latest" (rather than a better Earliest) is a more elegant path.

The refined behavior would be:

Out-of-range: Strictly follow latest semantics. This ensures a predictable "=
skip to end" behavior when users fall behind retention.

No-offset (Initial Start & Expansion): Leverage Group Creation Time for look=
up.

=E2=80=A2 For new groups, this naturally results in latest behavior since cr=
eation time is "now".

=E2=80=A2 For existing groups discovering new partitions, this results in ea=
rliest behavior for those specific partitions.

Group GC: If a group is purged, it is treated as a brand-new group with a cr=
eation time of "now," consistently skipping to the end.

WDYT?


