>=20
> =EF=BB=BFHi Jun,
>=20
> Thanks for the feedback. I agree that shifting this policy toward a "Smart=
er Latest" (rather than a better Earliest) is a more elegant path.
>=20
> The refined behavior would be:
>=20
> Out-of-range: Strictly follow latest semantics. This ensures a predictable=
 "skip to end" behavior when users fall behind retention.
>=20
> No-offset (Initial Start & Expansion): Leverage Group Creation Time for lo=
okup.
>=20
> =E2=80=A2 For new groups, this naturally results in latest behavior since c=
reation time is "now".
>=20
> =E2=80=A2 For existing groups discovering new partitions, this results in e=
arliest behavior for those specific partitions.
>=20
> Group GC: If a group is purged, it is treated as a brand-new group with a c=
reation time of "now," consistently skipping to the end.
>=20
> WDYT?
>=20
>=20
