> chia1: We should keep in mind that this could eventually be renamed to
> just "memberEpoch," and every rename requires actual changes in the
> user code (as opposed to renaming RPCs), so this could factor into
> whether we need the intermediate "generationIdOrMemberEpoch". Not
> strictly against it though.

Yes, renaming the method multiple times is definitely not ideal. My point was=
 that the public API is currently stale, and it would be more readable to sho=
w the correct and modern name. Maybe we could introduce memberEpoch() and dep=
recate generationId() with some helpful documentation.

BTW, it could be a separate KIP

Best,
Chia-Ping

On 2026/04/23 13:34:12 Lucas Brutschy via dev wrote:
> Thanks David. This is a nice improvement and I am in favour. I don't
