Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20526) Add ListClientConnections Admin API
 to list authenticated connections on brokers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Mehari Beyene (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Mehari Beyene created KAFKA-20526:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Add ListClientConnections Admin API to list authentic=
ated connections on brokers
                 Key: KAFKA-20526
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20526
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
          Components: clients, core
            Reporter: Mehari Beyene


h3. Motivation

Kafka brokers authenticate every client connection and store the authentica=
ted principal (KafkaPrincipal) in memory on each KafkaChannel. However, the=
re is *no admin API, CLI command, or JMX MBean* that allows an operator to =
answer:
{quote}Which user principals currently have active connections to this brok=
er?
{quote}
This is a fundamental observability gap. Every comparable system provides t=
his capability:
||System||Command / API||
|MySQL|{{SHOW PROCESSLIST}}|
|PostgreSQL|{{pg_stat_activity}}|
|RabbitMQ|Management API {{/api/connections}}|
|MongoDB|{{db.currentOp()}}|
|Apache Kafka|*Nothing*|
h3. Use Cases
 * {*}Security incident response{*}: When a credential is compromised, oper=
ators cannot determine if the compromised user has active connections witho=
ut restarting brokers or using indirect workarounds.
 * {*}Credential rotation{*}: No way to verify old credentials are no longe=
r in use on active connections.
 * {*}Audit and compliance{*}: Regulatory requirements mandate reporting wh=
o is connected at any point in time.
 * {*}Debugging{*}: Correlating connections with authenticated identities d=
uring troubleshooting.

h3. Current State

The broker already holds all the data in memory:
{code:java}
SocketServer
  =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 NetworkProcessor (one per network thread)
        =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 Selector
              =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 channels: Map[String, KafkaChanne=
l]
                    =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 KafkaChannel
                          =E2=94=9C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 principal(): KafkaPri=
ncipal    =E2=86=90 authenticated user
                          =E2=94=9C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 socketAddress: InetAd=
dress      =E2=86=90 client IP
                          =E2=94=9C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 channelMetadataRegist=
ry
                          =E2=94=82     =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 clientI=
nformation         =E2=86=90 software name/version
                          =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 id: String           =
           =E2=86=90 connection ID
{code}
The data is simply not surfaced through any external interface.
h3. Proposed Change

Add a new {{ListClientConnections}} admin API (broker-level RPC) that retur=
ns information about all currently authenticated connections on the target =
broker.

*Request fields:*
* {{PrincipalFilter}} (optional string) =E2=80=94 filter by principal name
* {{ClientAddressFilter}} (optional string) =E2=80=94 filter by client IP

*Response fields per connection:*
* {{ConnectionId}} =E2=80=94 the connection ID string
* {{Principal}} =E2=80=94 authenticated principal (e.g. {{User:alice}})
* {{ClientAddress}} =E2=80=94 remote client IP
* {{ClientPort}} =E2=80=94 remote client port
* {{ListenerName}} =E2=80=94 the listener the client connected to
* {{SecurityProtocol}} =E2=80=94 PLAINTEXT, SSL, SASL_PLAINTEXT, or SASL_SS=
L
* {{SoftwareName}} =E2=80=94 client software name (from KIP-511)
* {{SoftwareVersion}} =E2=80=94 client software version=C2=A0

A formal KIP will follow with complete request/response schemas and impleme=
ntation details.



