Ranidu Nethma created KAFKA-20529:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Remove aggressive hover animation from the ASF Feathe=
r logo on the Kafka website footer
                 Key: KAFKA-20529
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20529
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients
            Reporter: Ranidu Nethma
         Attachments: Screencast from 2026-04-27 10-34-29.webm

*Current Behavior:*

The Apache Software Foundation (ASF) feather logo on the kafka website foot=
er currently has a rapid continuous spin animation triggered on hover. The =
animation duration is set to {{{}0.2s{}}}, which causes the logo to rotate =
at a very high frequency.

=C2=A0

*CSS identified in the codebase:*
{code:java}
// ASF Feather Logo styling - Smaller with very rapid continuous spin
=20
effect.asf-feather-logo { =20
  max-width: 50px; =20
  width: 50px; =20
  height: auto; =20
  opacity: 0.7; =20
  transition: opacity 0.3s ease;

  &:hover {   =20
    opacity: 1;   =20
    animation: spin-continuous 0.2s linear infinite; =20
  }
} {code}
*Reason for Change:*
 # High speed spinning animations can detract from the professional aesthet=
ic of the Apache Kafka project site.

 # Most ASF project sites maintain a static or subtly transitioning logo.

=C2=A0

*Proposed Solution:*

Remove the {{animation: spin-continuous}} property from the {{.asf-feather-=
logo:hover}} selector.=C2=A0



